<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  Ikee_Tuning.xml                           Jawa_Patches - new file 2026-08-23
  ============================================================================

  THE IKEE BECOMES THE JAWA'S PET. Owner's brief, 2026-08-23:
  "the Ikee are the creepy Eyeling that we want to make into a Jawa pet. Modify
   the Ikee to be only a third of its current size. Give it the ability to
   nuzzle four times a day, yet have it be very messy all over (disgusting).
   Have it be very easy to train."

  🔑 The RENAME lives in Ikee_Rename.xml and is a separate concern. This file
  only changes what the animal IS. Read that file first for why the name is
  Ikee and for the wildAnimals dictionary-key trap.

  WHAT ALPHA ANIMALS SHIPS, measured from capture 2026-08-23T07-12-04Z:
      baseBodySize 0.4 · baseHealthScale 0.5 · wildness 0.2
      trainability Intermediate · nuzzleMtbHours -1 (NEVER) · petness 0
      manhunterOnDamageChance 0.5 · drawSize 1 / 1.25 / 1.5 by life stage
      MoveSpeed 3 · Mass 60 · a toxic sting at power 8

  ⚠️ nuzzleMtbHours -1 IS THE VANILLA "NEVER" SENTINEL, not a small number.
  It has to become a positive mean-time-between-events in HOURS. Four nuzzles
  a day means one per six hours, so 6.

  ⚠️ "VERY EASY TO TRAIN" IS TWO FIELDS AND THEY DO DIFFERENT JOBS.
  `wildness` is how hard it is to TAME and to keep tame; `trainability` is the
  CEILING on what it can ever learn. A low wildness with Intermediate
  trainability gives a pet that tames instantly and can never learn Rescue or
  Haul. Both move here.

  ⚠️ THE MESSINESS HAS NO RaceProperties FIELD. There is no `filthProducedPerDay`
  or equivalent on RaceProperties - checked across all 2,524 animal defs in the
  live set. RimWorld's own animal filth is driven by body size in
  Pawn_FilthTracker and is not exposed to XML, and making the Ikee SMALLER would
  have made it CLEANER. So the filth is added deliberately with
  CompProperties_Spawner, which is vanilla and is proven on pawns: the Dryads
  (Dryad_Woodmaker, Dryad_Berrymaker, Dryad_Medicinemaker) all carry one.
  Filth_Slime is chosen over Filth_AnimalFilth because it takes 70 work to clean
  against ordinary filth, lasts 35-40 days, and can attach to pawns walking
  through it - it is the disgusting option, not merely the dirty one.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- ==================================================================
       1. A THIRD OF ITS SIZE - body, health, mass and the drawn sprite
       ================================================================== -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods><li>Alpha Animals</li></mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AA_Eyeling"]/race/baseBodySize</xpath>
          <value><baseBodySize>0.13</baseBodySize></value>
        </li>

        <!-- 0.5 -> 0.35, not 0.17. A third of the HEALTH would make a pet that
             dies to a stray spark, and the owner asked for a posterchild, not a
             tragedy. Small and fragile, still keepable. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AA_Eyeling"]/race/baseHealthScale</xpath>
          <value><baseHealthScale>0.35</baseHealthScale></value>
        </li>

        <!-- a third the size carries a third the mass. 60 -> 20.
             🔑 CONDITIONAL, not a bare Replace: this node is NOT authored in
             Races_Eyeling.xml - it is inherited from AnimalThingBase or written by
             another mod's patch - so a Replace matches 0 nodes on disk and would be
             a silent no-op depending on load order. Replace it if present, add it if not. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AA_Eyeling"]/statBases/Mass</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
            <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AA_Eyeling"]/statBases/Mass</xpath>
            <value><Mass>20</Mass></value>
          </match>
          <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
            <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AA_Eyeling"]/statBases</xpath>
            <value><Mass>20</Mass></value>
          </nomatch>
        </li>

        <!-- ⚠️ drawSize is on the PawnKindDef's lifeStages, NOT on the ThingDef's
             graphicData - the ThingDef carries no graphicData at all. Three life
             stages, each divided by three: 1 / 1.25 / 1.5 -> 0.33 / 0.42 / 0.5 -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="AA_Eyeling"]/lifeStages/li[1]/bodyGraphicData/drawSize</xpath>
          <value><drawSize>0.33</drawSize></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="AA_Eyeling"]/lifeStages/li[2]/bodyGraphicData/drawSize</xpath>
          <value><drawSize>0.42</drawSize></value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="AA_Eyeling"]/lifeStages/li[3]/bodyGraphicData/drawSize</xpath>
          <value><drawSize>0.5</drawSize></value>
        </li>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             2. NUZZLES FOUR TIMES A DAY, and is a pet at all
             ================================================================== -->
        <!-- FOUR NUZZLES A DAY = one per six hours. -1 is the vanilla NEVER sentinel.
             🔑 CONDITIONAL, not a bare Replace: this node is NOT authored in
             Races_Eyeling.xml - it is inherited from AnimalThingBase or written by
             another mod's patch - so a Replace matches 0 nodes on disk and would be
             a silent no-op depending on load order. Replace it if present, add it if not. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AA_Eyeling"]/race/nuzzleMtbHours</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
            <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AA_Eyeling"]/race/nuzzleMtbHours</xpath>
            <value><nuzzleMtbHours>6</nuzzleMtbHours></value>
          </match>
          <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
            <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AA_Eyeling"]/race</xpath>
            <value><nuzzleMtbHours>6</nuzzleMtbHours></value>
          </nomatch>
        </li>

        <!-- petness 0 means it can NEVER bond, which would have made every other
             change here cosmetic. 0.9 is above the husky (0.75); this thing is
             meant to imprint on a Jawa and stay imprinted. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AA_Eyeling"]/race</xpath>
          <value><petness>0.9</petness></value>
        </li>

        <!-- a pet that turns manhunter on 50% of damage is not a pet. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AA_Eyeling"]/race</xpath>
          <value><manhunterOnDamageChance>0.02</manhunterOnDamageChance></value>
        </li>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             3. VERY EASY TO TRAIN - both halves
             ================================================================== -->
        <!-- how hard it is to TAME and to keep tame. 0.2 -> 0.02, easier than a cat.
             ⚠️ wildness is a StatDef (RimWorld.StatDefOf.Wildness), read via
             GetStatValueAbstract - it lives in statBases as <Wildness>, never
             under <race>. A value written into <race>/wildness is an unknown
             field the loader silently discards (measured: AA_Eyeling shipped
             statBases already declares Wildness 0.2, per Races_Eyeling.xml). -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AA_Eyeling"]/statBases/Wildness</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
            <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AA_Eyeling"]/statBases/Wildness</xpath>
            <value><Wildness>0.02</Wildness></value>
          </match>
          <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
            <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AA_Eyeling"]/statBases</xpath>
            <value><Wildness>0.02</Wildness></value>
          </nomatch>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AA_Eyeling"]/race/trainability</xpath>
          <value><trainability>Advanced</trainability></value>
        </li>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             4. VERY MESSY ALL OVER - see the header for why this is a comp
             ================================================================== -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AA_Eyeling"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <comps>
              <li Class="CompProperties_Spawner">
                <thingToSpawn>Filth_Slime</thingToSpawn>
                <spawnCount>1</spawnCount>
                <spawnIntervalRange>900~2200</spawnIntervalRange>
                <spawnMaxAdjacent>6</spawnMaxAdjacent>
                <spawnForbidden>true</spawnForbidden>
              </li>
            </comps>
          </value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
